std::list<int>::push_back under libc++ 18 ([list.modifiers]).  The verdict
is wrong: after `l.push_back(42)' size() and back() are nondet.
push_back (list:807, "symbol '__as_link' is unknown"), back (list:796,
"symbol '__prev_' is unknown") and clear (list:526, "symbol '__next_' is
unknown") are dropped, and one system-header declaration is dropped
before them: the members of the node types (__list_node_base's
__prev_/__next_, __list_node's __as_link) are not found, which points at
the node base class template, whose link-pointer member types are
__conditional_t / __rebind_pointer_t aliases over the node traits
(list:273-300), failing to complete.  A header-free imitation of that
typedef chain passes; test.desc is the header-free reduction
(alias-template substitution instantiates the pointee).
